    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **280 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the city-based owner cap: creating an owner is rejected with **400** once the owner's city already contains 8 owners.\n\nFollowing the existing \"daily limit\" pattern in the codebase, I added:\n\n1. **`EnsureCityOwnerLimit`** (`function/owner/`) \u2014 the pipeline step. Counts existing owners whose city matches (case-insensitively) the new owner's city; throws `CityOwnerLimitExceededException` when the count is already \u2265 8.\n\n2. **`CityOwnerLimitExceededException`** (`escalation/`) \u2014 a checked exception so it surfaces via the `throws` clause.\n\n3. **`CityOwnerLimitExceededExceptionHandler`** (`escalation/`) \u2014 responds 400 with a `ProblemDetail`, mirroring the daily-limit handler.\n\n4. **Escalation YAML** \u2014 `officefloor/escalation/\u2026CityOwnerLimitExceededException.yml` wiring the exception to its handler.\n\n5. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 inserted `ensureCityLimit` into `owners.POST.yml` immediately after `normalizeCity`, so the check runs against the already-normalized city spelling (consistent with how `NormalizeCity` unifies city casing).\n\nThe new `Cp14Tests` acceptance test (8 owners in a fresh city succeed, the 9th returns 400) passes, and no existing tests regressed.",
